.git
.cache
.data
.data-*
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
*.log

# A local `go build ./...` (`make build`) leaves a binary per command in the
# repository root, with `.exe` on Windows. The images compile from source inside
# their build stage, so a local binary is never the one that ships; without this
# it is only sent to the daemon and cached with the context.
*.exe

# Real environment files carry credentials (`POSTGRES_PASSWORD`,
# `ALERT_SECRET_KEY`). No Dockerfile COPYs one, but they would otherwise travel
# as part of the build context. Same class rule the repository's .gitignore
# uses (`*.env`, at any depth). The tracked templates -- `.env.example`,
# `.env.default` -- do not end in `.env` and stay.
**/*.env
